              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DeniseKantner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Light, delicious and just perfect! I added 1/2 cup coconut to the mix. As our youngest daughter used to say, \"all gone!\""
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary-Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is extremely close to a wonderful Weight Watchers recipe I used to use back in the late 90's! So happy to have found it again! I use canned mandarin oranges (no sugar added) and the red/white grapefruit you can get in a jar (refrigerated). It's so much easier than trying to cut out the sections from the whole fruit! \n\nI use a little less butter, and a mix of brown sugar and sugar substitute. To top it off I add a few tablespoons of chopped pecans! Wonderful and only 3 points for a 1/2 cup serving! Great warm as is or as a topping on low fat frozen vanilla yogurt!",
            "datePublished": "2013-09-21T07:54:59.820Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "spice of life"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious. Made with grapefruit from my own tree. Added three oranges and a little over a cup of fresh pineapple. Delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-20T11:09:56.590Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I served this dessert as a warmed topping on lemon sorbet. To make it healthier, instead of 1/2 Cup of sugar, I used 1 teaspoon of organic sucanat dried sugar cane juice (a brown sugar). It was light and refreshing.",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-06T18:18:28.290Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mrs kosmos"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If you're looking for a sweet dessert, this isn't it. If you're looking for a tasty and different fruit salad, this is perfect. We also added 1/2 C coconut to the topping mix like DeniseKanter suggested, and the coconut made it extra tasty. We probably would have rated it only 3 stars without the coconut. I'll probably regularly start making this whenever we get grapefruit in our CSA box, but since I'm not a huge grapefruit fan, in the future, I'll probably up the orange and pineapple and reduce the grapefruit.",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-16T18:10:39.143Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heather Pulley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We enjoyed this dish a lot, although we served it as part of our meal rather than dessert! I used canned pineapple and diced up my oranges and grapefruit.",
